---
metadata: {
    partial_name: "Account | Safe Return To",
}
---
{%- comment -%}
  Returns path when it is a path on this site, otherwise blank. Called with:
    function return_to = 'modules/dashboard/account/safe_return_to', path: context.params.return_to
  Allowed: starts with a single / (not // and not /\), contains no backslash or control character.
  The 2FA pages themselves and .json endpoints are excluded to prevent redirect loops.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign path = path | default: '' | append: '' | strip
  assign first_char = path | slice: 0, 1
  assign second_char = path | slice: 1, 1
  comment
    Liquid strings cannot hold a backslash, so look for its encoded form (%5C).
  endcomment
  assign encoded_path = path | url_encode

  if first_char != '/' or second_char == '/' or encoded_path contains '%5C'
    return ''
  endif

  comment
    No control characters (tab, newline and the like): the redirect tag errors on them.
    Encoded, they are %00 to %1F and %7F. A literal % is encoded as %25, so it cannot match.
  endcomment
  if encoded_path contains '%0' or encoded_path contains '%1' or encoded_path contains '%7F'
    return ''
  endif

  assign bare_path = path | split: '?' | first
  if bare_path == '/verify-2fa' or bare_path == '/account/2fa' or path contains '.json'
    return ''
  endif

  return path
-%}
